WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.280
- We've got one final uplifting story

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:03.360
to close out this hour.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.900
This is "What I'm Liking."
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.960
TV meteorologists are known
for getting a bit creative

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.360
with their weather
forecasts from time to time.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.720
And as we finish up a show
dedicated to a popular book

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.210
I wanna share what one
Nashville Meteorologist did

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:22.020
during a recent broadcast to
reinforce the power of reading.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.310
- Hi everyone, I'm Henry Rothenberg

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.290
with a favorite book forecast.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.870
It's definitely not "Cloudy
with a Chance of Meatballs."

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:31.170
As that sunshine helped us
get almost to a hundred today

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:34.260
breaking the record high
temperature, Tuesday.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.760
And that made for a no good

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.250
very bad day for folks
that are ready for fall

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.640
those upper nineties to
around 100 across the region.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.250
It's really been a series
of unfortunate events

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.110
with the "Charlotte's Web" of humidity.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:49.350
these humid conditions
all across the region.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.210
But know you aren't in a wrinkle

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:56.210
of time as we're days away from
the official start of fall.

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:59.520
- Oh my gosh, that's News
Channel five's Henry Rothenberg.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.340
He packed in nearly a dozen
children's book references

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.600
in his two minute segment.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:04.650
I've literally read 'em all those

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.990
with my kids and it was
all for a good cause.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:10.440
We have Henry on the line
to explain what's up Henry?

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.120
- Hey Kelly, how you doing today?

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.873
- I'm doing so great, man.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:14.706
It's great to meet you,

00:01:14.706 --> 00:01:17.100
so tell us about that special segment.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:21.180
- Well, Scripps Howard Fund,
which is the philanthropic arm

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.790
of the E.W. Scripps Company
who owns Channel Five here

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.580
in Nashville seven years
ago, started this campaign.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.250
If you give a child a
book and it's so simple

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.440
you don't think about the
fact that there are a lot

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.570
of children that don't
own a book of their own.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.100
They don't have a single book.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.740
So, Scripps and News Channel
five and our stations

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.260
around the country started this campaign

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.390
allowing people to donate money

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.900
so that we can have these book
fairs in Title one schools

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:49.650
which in turn make sure that
children get at least one book

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.750
of their own that they can take home.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:53.490
And it's an incredible program.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:54.750
The picture that you just saw there

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.280
that little girl I'll never forget

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.990
that was the first one I ever did.

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:00.360
She got that book she ran to checkout

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.010
cost them no money, then ran back

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.975
sat in my lap started to
read it to her right there.

00:02:03.975 --> 00:02:05.550
- Aw, I love that.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:07.710
You say that this is more important now

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.810
than ever in Nashville, why so?

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.010
- Especially in Nashville.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.900
You know, you think about
the last two and a half years

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:13.980
we've all been through a lot

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.130
but we had the devastating
tornadoes of March 2020,

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:18.600
two weeks after that,

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.910
the world shut down to a global pandemic.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.340
So, children this school year especially

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:26.190
are just now getting back into a routine.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:27.600
And I'm really proud to say

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.240
that this school year News
Channel five will hand

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:33.600
out our 10,000th book and
the Scripps Howard Fund

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:35.610
across the country this
school year will hand

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:37.500
out their 1,000,000th book.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.477
And of course, if anybody
would like to help donate

00:02:40.477 --> 00:02:44.010
$5 can put one book in a child's hand.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:48.030
You can go to newschannel5.com/giveabook

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:51.350
or you can text NC five,

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.280
to 5 0 1 5 5.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.370
And again, all it takes
is $5 to put one book

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.360
in a child's hand.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.380
- That is incredible.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.730
Thank you so much, Henry.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.411
I'm liking your post right now.

00:03:01.411 --> 00:03:02.408
(chime)
(audience applause)

00:03:02.408 --> 00:03:03.330
And that's not all our season long

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.160
partner pilot pen makers of FriXion,

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.050
the go to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.990
want to celebrate the power
of reading just like you, sir.

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:11.460
So they're gonna give the

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:15.233
if you give a child a
book campaign $1,000.

00:03:15.233 --> 00:03:17.250
(applause)

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:20.430
and if you at home want
to donate to the campaign

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.560
you can learn more on our Insta story.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.600
Thank you so much to
all of our guests today.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.155
Mila Kunis, Chiara Aurelia, Jessica Knoll,

00:03:27.155 --> 00:03:29.850
(indistinct) and Tink.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.400
I just wanna take a moment
to honor a true legend.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.770
This week, the world lost
the Queen of Country,

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:35.910
Miss Loretta Lynn

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:38.550
and I don't say queen
lightly, she was literally

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.310
the most awarded female
country artist of all times

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.140
She had dozens of number one songs

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.140
like Coal Miner's Daughter
and You Ain't Woman Enough.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.240
It's not just her music

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.700
but her presence and
grace that will endure.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.650
Thank you so much to Loretta Lynn

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:55.049
for all that you gave to us.

00:03:55.049 --> 00:03:57.632
(somber music)

